WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Heart and circulatory disease.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:08.020
In the UK in 1961, it caused
more than half of all deaths:

3
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.270
320,000 of them.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.510
Today, it causes about
170,000 deaths a year:

5
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.050
about 26 per cent of all UK deaths.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.850
Yet over 8 million people in
the UK are living with it.

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.750
So why has its death rate fallen so far?

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.530
Did people's genes change?

9
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.770
In this mission, you'll map where early
deaths from it are highest and lowest

10
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.530
across the UK.

11
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:38.050
Then you'll compare how the NHS,
charities and world agencies fight back.

12
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.790
Your mission: explain why the UK's death
rate from heart and circulatory disease

13
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.510
has fallen so far.
